## Bug Diagnosis (with line evidence)

### Bug 1 — Rubber-band drag only selects the last found keyframe
**Location:** `Gui/FluxTimeline.cpp:3030–3068` (`selectKeyframesInRect`)

**Root cause:** The vertical overlap test compares a **content-local Y** (`vr.y`) against **screen/widget Y** (`normalized.top()` / `normalized.bottom()`).

```cpp
// Line ~3044
rowY = vr.y;                         // content-local: starts at 0
rowH = vr.height;

// Line ~3054
if (rowY + rowH < normalized.top() || rowY > normalized.bottom()) continue;
```

`vr.y` is the un-scrolled content offset assigned in `rebuildVisibleRows()`. `normalized` comes from the rubber-band rectangle, whose coordinates are in widget space (e.g., `y ≥ kTimeRulerHeight` when below the ruler). Because `rowY` is not adjusted by `kTimeRulerHeight - _scrollOffsetY`, the check rejects every row whose content Y is smaller than the screen Y of the rubber band. Only rows with large `rowY` values—typically the bottom-most visible property rows—pass the test, so only their keyframes are appended to `_selectedKeys`.

**Fix:** Convert `rowY` to screen coordinates before the overlap test:
```cpp
int screenRowY = kTimeRulerHeight + rowY - _scrollOffsetY;
if (screenRowY + rowH < normalized.top() || screenRowY > normalized.bottom()) continue;
```

