### Bug 2 — Selection box only appears inside the keyframed timeline area
**Location:** `Gui/FluxTimeline.cpp:3647–3698` (`mousePressEvent`)

**Root cause:** `eModeRubberBandSelect` is only initiated when the click lands on **empty space in a property row** (`eFluxVisibleRowProperty`). The relevant gate:

```cpp
if (clickRow && clickRow->type == eFluxVisibleRowProperty) {
    ...
    // Click on empty space in property row
    if (!ctrlHeld) {
        _interactionMode = eModeRubberBandSelect;
        _rubberBandStart = QPoint(x, y);
        _rubberBandCurrent = QPoint(x, y);
    }
}
```

If the user clicks on a layer bar, effect row, mask row, text-animator row, empty space below all visible rows (where `yToRow` returns `nullptr` and the code falls through to playhead drag), or the time ruler, rubber-band mode is **never entered**. Once the mode *is* started, `mouseMoveEvent` does not clamp coordinates and `paintEvent` does not clip the rectangle, but the user cannot initiate the drag from most of the widget surface. This effectively confines rubber-band selection to the property-row area.

