### Bug 3 — Multiselect drag only moves the keyframe under the mouse
**Location:** `Gui/FluxTimeline.cpp:3663–3676` (`mousePressEvent`)

**Root cause:** On a regular (non-Ctrl) click on a keyframe diamond, the code **unconditionally clears** `_selectedKeys` instead of checking whether the clicked keyframe is already part of the existing multi-selection.

```cpp
if (nearestKeyTimeForProperty(prop, xToFrame(x), toleranceFrames, &nearestTime)) {
    if (ctrlHeld) {
        toggleKeyframeSelection(propIdx, nearestTime);
    } else {
        _selectedKeys.clear();                                 // ← always wipes multi-select
        _selectedKeys.append(SelectedKeyframe(propIdx, nearestTime));
        _selectedKeyPropertyIndex = propIdx;
        _selectedKeyTime = nearestTime;
        _interactionMode = eModeDragKeyframe;                  // ← now drags only this key
        ...
    }
}
```

Because `_selectedKeys` is cleared, a previously rubber-band-selected set is destroyed. When `mouseReleaseEvent` later handles `eModeDragKeyframe`, it iterates `_selectedKeys` and moves only the single key that was just added.

**Fix:** Check if the clicked key is already selected before clearing. If it is, enter `eModeDragKeyframe` with the existing `_selectedKeys` intact:

```cpp
} else if (isKeyframeSelected(propIdx, nearestTime)) {
    // Already in multi-select — drag all selected keys
    _interactionMode = eModeDragKeyframe;
    _interactionStartX = x;
    _interactionStartY = y;
    _dragPropertyIndex = propIdx;
    _dragOrigKeyTime = nearestTime;
    _dragCurrentKeyTime = nearestTime;
    clearSnapState();
    _snapShiftHeld = (QApplication::keyboardModifiers() & Qt::ShiftModifier) != 0;
    setCursor(Qt::SplitHCursor);
} else {
    _selectedKeys.clear();
    _selectedKeys.append(SelectedKeyframe(propIdx, nearestTime));
    ...
}
```